WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.930
Larry David has spent more than a decade railing
against social slights both real and imagined

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.260
on Curb Your Enthusiasm.

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:10.780
The sort-of-biographical character proved
that misanthropy can be very funny, albeit

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.260
pretty annoying at some points.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.320
And while audiences were entertained by all
those awkward encounters, a lot of Curb's

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.700
characters got pretty disrespected by his
bonehead behavior on the show.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.340
"Ya had to interfere didn't ya?"

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.540
Here are the worst things Larry David ever
did on Curb Your Enthusiasm.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.000
Yes, step-fathers count

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.540
Empathy doesn't come easily to the Curb version
of Larry David.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.120
That's one of the reasons why we love him.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.860
And Larry's complete inability to give a crap
can even push him a little too far, as in

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.180
the first season finale, "The Group."

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.470
In the episode, Larry runs into an old flame
who asks Larry to accompany her to an incest

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.960
survivor's group … and of course, he makes
it weird.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.040
When Larry learns that Lisa was molested by
her stepfather, his reaction is less than

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:51.540
supportive.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.240
"Are you sure that you qualify for the stepfather,
is that considered incest?"

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.160
"Oh Larry."

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.300
And while sitting in on the therapy session,
he invents a story about an uncle who molested

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.060
him as a child.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:07.360
"My name is Todd, and I'm an incest survivor."

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.820
By the end of the episode, the group's leader
comes face to face with Larry's actual uncle

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.280
and promptly rips him apart in front of everyone.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.340
Yikes.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.120
The Tivo tipping point

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:21.220
Even Larry's long-suffering wife Cheryl had
to call it quits eventually.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.260
In Season 7, after finding herself on a wildly
turbulent flight, Cheryl calls Larry to say

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.560
goodbye for what she thinks might be forever.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.840
But Larry's too distracted by his TV repairman
to listen to her.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.420
"Call me back in ten minutes."

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.800
For Cheryl, that's it.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.540
It's not just the phone call, of course …

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.160
"What else is it about?"

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.800
"What else is it about?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:40.980
It's all of it."

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.380
"You can't do anything like a normal person."

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.760
But the TiVo incident is the straw that breaks
the camel's back, and leads her to file for

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.260
divorce.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.700
After that, most of the couple's mutual friends
side with Cheryl, throwing Larry's social

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.080
life into disarray, and his favorite restaurant
refuses to seat him.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.940
But the biggest tragedy to Larry?

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.780
The TiVo still doesn't work.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.680
Unwheelievable

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.290
Seinfeld's George Costanza is partially based
on Larry David, so it can be a little hard

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:07.660
to tell them apart sometimes.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.720
Just like when George faked a handicap to
get a job, Larry starts dating a woman in

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.260
a wheelchair...and uses it to his advantage.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.120
He starts out by saying — well, this:

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.880
"By the way, what's the proper term

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.390
Are you handicapped, are you disabled..

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.680
what's the word... Challenged?"

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.460
"Are you challenged?"

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.200
Then, in true Larry David fashion, he starts
using others' sympathy for her as a social

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.160
shield for himself.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.140
He then hits on another woman in a wheelchair
but runs into Denise at a party.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:41.040
So, instead of owning up to his own terrible
decisions, he sticks Wendy in a closet before

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.860
Denise discovers his dirty secret.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.240
"Who the hell is she?"

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.540
"Wendy Wheelchair?"

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.600
Needless to say, neither of those women ever
came back into the picture.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.020
Graverobber

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.840
You don't have to be among the living to suffer
Larry David's shenanigans.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.380
Marty Funkhouser, one of Larry's friends,
knows this all too well.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.760
Larry attends his father's open-casket funeral
and discovers that Marty's dad will be buried

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.540
with his prized golf club, which Larry also
loves.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:11.220
Instead of respecting the dead guy's wishes,
though, he switches the club out for a replacement.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.760
Annnnd everyone finds out about it in the
middle of service.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.080
Then, when Funkhouser's mother passes away,
Larry does it again.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.860
Not only does he literally laugh in Marty's
face when he expresses his grief …

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.500
"You can be a hundred and be an orphan."

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.260
"You can't be 100 and be an orphan."

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:25.760
"Yea you can."

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.500
"Ha, okay, little orphan Funkhouser."

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.459
… but he also proceeds to steal flowers
from the roadside memorial that's built near

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.730
the site of her car accident.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.740
Larry snags the bouquets to offer flowers
to people for free.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.640
Then he steals the dead lady's perfume to
give to Cheryl.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.320
And of course, Larry has no remorse.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.120
Because Funkhouser owed him 50 dollars anyway.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.980
For Christ's sake, Larry

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:52.540
Larry David incited a lot of religious ire
after, uh, peeing on Jesus.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.819
After he's prescribed a medication that makes
him urinate out of control, he accidentally

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:00.520
gets a drop of his pee on Jesus and decides
not to wipe it away.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:06.200
That's when the painting's owners think the
image is producing real tears, and chaos ensues.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.080
"Larry you sprayed on Jesus?"

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:10.480
Why, yes.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:11.460
Yes, he did.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.680
Thanks for watching!

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.160
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.510
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

